From 4bbfa87b44f3f35d41c877b31c0d109511f021af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 20:00:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add the multiframe batch driver

Frame N's trained splats, copied out of the engine in training space,
seed frame N+1, which refines them with no growth, relocation or MCMC
noise so the count and every splat's index stay fixed. Each frame is
written to ply/ and queued for SOG export on a worker thread, so the
palette k-means runs beside the next frame's training.

TrainerSession gains carried_splats, capture_splats() and
rebase_dataset(); the frames share the first frame's parsed cameras and
only swap their image, depth and normal paths.
